    ↓
Transformer (Inference Rules)
    ↓
Next-Token Prediction (Theorem Generation)
    ↓
Confidence Score (Fake Certainty)
```

**The Contradiction:**

| What the LLM Does | What This Requires |
| :--- | :--- |
| Generates statements | Truth conditions |
| Assigns probabilities | Actual frequencies |
| Produces confidence | Access to reality |
| Claims knowledge | Grounding |
| Spins narratives | Correspondence |

**The LLM has the form of knowledge without its substance.**

---

### Why This Causes Hallucinations

**Hallucination = Form without Substance**

The LLM can:
- ✅ Generate syntactically perfect sentences
- ✅ Maintain grammatical coherence
- ✅ Reference known entities
- ✅ Follow rhetorical structures
- ✅ Sound authoritative

The LLM cannot:
- ❌ Check if statements correspond to reality
- ❌ Access the referent of a word
- ❌ Distinguish truth from plausibility
- ❌ Ground claims in experience
- ❌ Recognize when it's fabricating

**It is the perfect simulation of knowledge—which is exactly what makes it produce hallucinations.**

